the meals occasionally.

00:02:34.463 --> 00:02:35.930
- Um.

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:38.010
- That's why they're interested
in trying new things.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:39.060
- Yeah, my daughter's always,

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:40.050
every time we're in the kitchen together,

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:41.250
she always wants to use the knife

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:42.610
and I'm like it's a little weird

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:44.480
how much you wanna use the knife.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:45.360
It's actually a little.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:46.630
- [Woman] Right.

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:48.290
- So are your kids into cooking?

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:49.920
Do they like it?

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:51.290
- Mine are more into it

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:52.803
if I was more into it.

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:55.520
Look, we have strengths and weaknesses

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:56.800
and mine is not in the kitchen.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:58.610
I'm gonna buy your book.
- Mine is not either.

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:00.440
- [Kelly] I'm gonna buy the book.

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:02.880
